# GitHub and local work context

When discussing roadmap, bugs, features, refactors, or what to do next:

1. Prefer reading `integrations/work-context.json` if it exists. It lists **all local repository files** under `localWorkFiles` together with **open GitHub pull requests and issues** (generated on the developer machine).
2. If that file is missing or clearly stale, suggest running `.\scripts\sync-workspace.ps1` from the repo root (requires [GitHub CLI](https://cli.github.com/) and `gh auth login`).
3. In pull requests, use the GitHub **linked issues** syntax in descriptions and commits (`Fixes #123`, `Relates to #456`) so work stays traceable.

The committed sample shape lives at `integrations/work-context.example.json` (minimal fields: four `localWorkFiles` paths — `index.html`, `invoice.html`, `review.html`, `docs/ROADMAP.md`; **pytest** enforces the exact set). A generated `integrations/work-context.json` lists all repo files under `localWorkFiles` and may include additional PR/issue properties returned by **GitHub CLI** (`gh`).

When editing **`docs/issues-backlog.md`**, **`.github/ISSUE_TEMPLATE/config.yml`** (including **Doc index (issues-backlog)** **`about`** ↔ **`issues-backlog.md`** orienting lines), **`review.html`** (Issues backlog cards, Documentation grid, **Python + desktop** body copy), **`index.html`** / **`invoice.html`** README hint lines, **`probooks/help_epilog.py`** (shared CLI/desktop **`--help`** Excel line), hub **Related docs** / **Other docs** / **README** **Docs** bar Excel segments, the shared **README — Default database paths** hub segment on **ROADMAP** / **BACKLOG** / **CONTRIBUTING** (**`test_hub_docs_related_docs_link_readme_default_database_paths`**), or the shared **issues-backlog.md** blurb on **ROADMAP** / **BACKLOG** / **CONTRIBUTING**, use **`docs/CONTRIBUTING.md`** (**[Continuous integration](https://github.com/johnnyachavez/ProBooksAi/blob/main/docs/CONTRIBUTING.md#continuous-integration)**) and **`tests/test_ci_validate_layout_sync.py`** so contract tests stay green. The **README — Excel workbook template** parenthetical on **ROADMAP** / **BACKLOG** / **CONTRIBUTING** hub **Related docs** / **Other docs** lines must stay verbatim-identical (**`test_hub_docs_related_docs_link_readme_excel_workbook_template`**).

When editing **`README.md`** **`### Default database paths (Windows)`** or the **ROADMAP** implementation snapshot **Why not one `.db` yet** / **#21** database notes, keep **README** ↔ **ROADMAP** aligned per **CONTRIBUTING.md** (**`test_readme_default_database_paths_notes_two_schemas_and_roadmap`**, **`test_pr_template_lists_readme_default_database_paths_checklist`**, **`test_contributing_ci_documents_readme_default_database_paths_bullet`**). **README** top **Docs** line should include **`#default-database-paths-windows`** (**`test_readme_docs_bar_links_default_database_paths_anchor`**). Root **`review.html`** (**Documentation** card + **Python + desktop** paragraph) must keep **`README.md#default-database-paths-windows`** in sync (**`test_review_html_readme_default_database_paths_documentation_card`**, **`test_review_html_links_readme_web_shell_and_desktop_anchors`**, **`test_review_html_python_desktop_section_mentions_help_epilog`**).

**Layout validators:** **`scripts/ci_validate_layout.sh`** and **`scripts/ci_validate_layout.ps1`** **`require`** this file (same path in both lists) and **`probooks/help_epilog.py`** (next to **`probooks/cli.py`**); the GitHub Actions **validate** job runs the **`.sh`** script.
